#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Live terminal monitor for all running Claude Code sessions on this machine.

Session list and status come from `claude agents --json`. Model, context size,
branch and current activity come from each session's transcript, whose format
is internal to Claude Code, so those fields may go blank after an update.

Usage: claude-monitor                     terminal view (up/down or j/k select, q quit)
       claude-monitor --web [--port N]    browser view with pixel-art agents
       claude-monitor --app               browser view in its own window; stops when it closes
       claude-monitor --once              print one snapshot
       claude-monitor --hook              Claude Code hook: records and announces "needs you" events
       claude-monitor --setup             add the hooks (and a status line, if there is none) to Claude Code
       claude-monitor --version           print the version

The browser views also show the screen of each running Android emulator, linked to
the session using it. To skip the emulator's own window, start it with -no-window.

On Windows there is no tmux, so sessions the app starts run in a small background
"session host" (claude-monitor --session-host) built on ConPTY. It keeps them alive
while the app restarts or updates, and exits once it has no sessions left.
"""
